  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal gas is enclosed in a cylinder at pressure of <math><mn>2</mn></math> atm and temperature, <math><mn>300</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The mean time between two successive collisions is <math><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msup><mi>s</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the pressure is doubled and temperature is increased to <math><mn>500</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the mean time between two successive collisions will be close to:",
